<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 27.35pt; text-align: justify"><b>&#160;</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><i>Sensitivity Analysis</i></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify">The fair value measurements are sensitive
to changes in significant unobservable inputs. For the warrant liabilities, increases in expected volatility or expected term would generally
result in a higher fair value measurement. For the convertible note, increases in the discount rate would generally result in a lower
fair value measurement. Management has determined that reasonably possible changes in these assumptions would not result in a material
change in the related fair value measurements. Therefore, no quantitative sensitivity analysis has been disclosed.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><b>Warrants issued in September 2025</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify">On January 27, 2026, the Company entered
into warrant repurchase agreements with certain holders of warrants originally issued in September 2025. Under the agreements, the Company
